(3081291, 433165, 49480, '<td valign="top">Man, people are going to start getting sick of seeing Taughannock.  A different time of day wouuld have worked better to avoid the lens flare.  I like how the water looks due to the long exposure.</td>', 'Man, people are going to start getting sick of seeing Taughannock.  A different time of day wouuld have worked better to avoid the lens flare.  I like how the water looks due to the long exposure.', '2006-12-02 09:26:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081302, 432989, 61138, '<td valign="top">Wow. Fantastic composition. You''ve made superb use of what I assume is a rare opportunity to shoot these two subjects in the same frame.<br/> <br/>I love the gentle gardient of light in the sky...the back-lighting of the opera house, and your careful cropping to squeeze every last pixel out of the image.<br/> <br/>I gave it a 9 at first, but I''m bumping it up to a 10.</td>', 'Wow. Fantastic composition. You''ve made superb use of what I assume is a rare opportunity to shoot these two subjects in the same frame. I love the gentle gardient of light in the sky...the back-lighting of the opera house, and your careful cropping to squeeze every last pixel out of the image. I gave it a 9 at first, but I''m bumping it up to a 10.', '2006-12-02 09:42:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081305, 432388, 64918, '<td valign="top">Great observational capture - the trees look like some kind of skeletal alien species! Great colour pallet too - love the muted tones. <br/>The sky area though kinda flattens it out a bit for me - it doesn''t feel like it''s contributing - I''d suggest cropping right down to just above the tree line so that the sky area balances with the water more... seems to increase the impression of a more dynamic perspective. <br/>Like this image - nice work.</td>', 'Great observational capture - the trees look like some kind of skeletal alien species! Great colour pallet too - love the muted tones. The sky area though kinda flattens it out a bit for me - it doesn''t feel like it''s contributing - I''d suggest cropping right down to just above the tree line so that the sky area balances with the water more... seems to increase the impression of a more dynamic perspective. Like this image - nice work.', '2006-12-02 09:50:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081306, 433541, 64918, '<td valign="top">Great portrait - like the way the highlights blow out to frame the image.</td>', 'Great portrait - like the way the highlights blow out to frame the image.', '2006-12-02 09:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081307, 433213, 61138, '<td valign="top">Precision capture! The stillness, and the knowledge of the imminent landing and accompanying turmoil, imbue this image with an amazing tension.<br/> <br/>Your timing was flawless. The detail is crisp and the cropping is right on the money. 9.</td>', 'Precision capture! The stillness, and the knowledge of the imminent landing and accompanying turmoil, imbue this image with an amazing tension. Your timing was flawless. The detail is crisp and the cropping is right on the money. 9.', '2006-12-02 09:51:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081308, 433558, 64918, '<td valign="top">Great image - love the attitude. Kinda has an ''antiquated'' feel to it.</td>', 'Great image - love the attitude. Kinda has an ''antiquated'' feel to it.', '2006-12-02 09:53:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081312, 429824, 64918, '<td valign="top">Spooky - I can imagine Excaliber being thrust out of the water at any minute!. A knight on a white charger might have increased the Arthurian impact a bit more than the sheep but they''re never about when you need them - and maybe it''s a killer sheep finishing off the remains of it''s last victim.<br/>Great colours - just noticed the sky has a hint of ''Turner'' about it too - very atmospheric and surreal.</td>', 'Spooky - I can imagine Excaliber being thrust out of the water at any minute!. A knight on a white charger might have increased the Arthurian impact a bit more than the sheep but they''re never about when you need them - and maybe it''s a killer sheep finishing off the remains of it''s last victim.Great colours - just noticed the sky has a hint of ''Turner'' about it too - very atmospheric and surreal.', '2006-12-02 09:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081320, 432818, 64918, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition and lighting on this - use of the shadows as a major element in the foreground works really well.</td>', 'Excellent composition and lighting on this - use of the shadows as a major element in the foreground works really well.', '2006-12-02 10:03:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081325, 428018, 64918, '<td valign="top">Love the colours and feeling of senerity. <br/>Would suggest maybe cropping out the water at the bottom - it kind of breaks into the muted colours and removing it also gives the impression that the bridge is much higher up (above a deep gorge or something) which I feel adds to the atmosphere. The guy in the yellow jacket is a great capture!</td>', 'Love the colours and feeling of senerity. Would suggest maybe cropping out the water at the bottom - it kind of breaks into the muted colours and removing it also gives the impression that the bridge is much higher up (above a deep gorge or something) which I feel adds to the atmosphere. The guy in the yellow jacket is a great capture!', '2006-12-02 10:07:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081329, 426217, 64918, '<td valign="top">Formidable - something that Mervyn Peake might draw. Feels like a character out of a novel - great mood.</td>', 'Formidable - something that Mervyn Peake might draw. Feels like a character out of a novel - great mood.', '2006-12-02 10:08:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081332, 431788, 64918, '<td valign="top">Great capture... cropping out the little girl leaves the image with some beautiful flowing lines - almost abstract in that you can still see what it is but it''s more about movement and gracefulness and awesome power. Wonderful colours.</td>', 'Great capture... cropping out the little girl leaves the image with some beautiful flowing lines - almost abstract in that you can still see what it is but it''s more about movement and gracefulness and awesome power. Wonderful colours.', '2006-12-02 10:11:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081334, 425030, 64918, '<td valign="top">Have I seen this one/similar somewhere recently? B/w? <br/>Whatever, it works beautifully in colour - the lighting on the church is very dramatic and arresting. <br/>The only thing I''d suggest is that the foreground gravel seems to be overly sharpened - i like the idea of it having a very gritty feel to it but flattens out the depth in the foreground for me. A more blended foreground may improve the flow in this area I feel.</td>', 'Have I seen this one/similar somewhere recently? B/w? Whatever, it works beautifully in colour - the lighting on the church is very dramatic and arresting. The only thing I''d suggest is that the foreground gravel seems to be overly sharpened - i like the idea of it having a very gritty feel to it but flattens out the depth in the foreground for me. A more blended foreground may improve the flow in this area I feel.', '2006-12-02 10:17:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3081337, 433074, 64918, '<td valign="top">Nicely captured!</td>', 'Nicely captured!', '2006-12-02 10:18:17.000000', NULL, 1),
