(3100121, 423136, 27735, '<td valign="top">Thanks! El Capitan is located just right of the frame. I stacked a couple of graduated neutral density filters to keep the real and the reflected properly exposed.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Absolutely beautiful!  I''m in awe (and a bit jealous I have to admit).  Great timing on the lighting for this.  It''s funny how those reflections work when the angle and height of the camera can really alter what''s reflected (i.e. - the height of the tree in the bottom right reflection appears taller than the background mountain, but not the "right side-up" part of it).  I also like how you''ve maintained the deep blue in both the top and bottom sections of this image.  Anyway, well done and congratulations in advance on what should be a fine score.  :D </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks! El Capitan is located just right of the frame. I stacked a couple of graduated neutral density filters to keep the real and the reflected properly exposed. Originally posted by glad2badad: Absolutely beautiful!  I''m in awe (and a bit jealous I have to admit).  Great timing on the lighting for this.  It''s funny how those reflections work when the angle and height of the camera can really alter what''s reflected (i.e. - the height of the tree in the bottom right reflection appears taller than the background mountain, but not the "right side-up" part of it).  I also like how you''ve maintained the deep blue in both the top and bottom sections of this image.  Anyway, well done and congratulations in advance on what should be a fine score.  :D ', '2006-12-08 14:10:32.000000', NULL, 0),
