(3102931, 430423, 43410, '<td valign="top">great shot, i really like this.  don''t be discouraged.  it''s your second highest scoring picture, and they''ll only get better.  sometimes it''s hard to understand why it didn''t do as well as you think it should have (been there done that multiple times), but just learn from it.  you have some amazing work in your portfolio.  great job on a wonderful animal.  can''t wait to see him in the Pet Portrait as well :D</td>', 'great shot, i really like this.  don''t be discouraged.  it''s your second highest scoring picture, and they''ll only get better.  sometimes it''s hard to understand why it didn''t do as well as you think it should have (been there done that multiple times), but just learn from it.  you have some amazing work in your portfolio.  great job on a wonderful animal.  can''t wait to see him in the Pet Portrait as well :D', '2006-12-09 19:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3102941, 431443, 53278, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ElGordo:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent work!  Your IR image really shows off the foliage well.  How did you manage to keep the sky such a beautiful blue? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i took many many shots with different aperture/exposure time.<br/>shot in raw, white balance in photoshop (incadescent), auto levels, and channel inversion. and hue /saturation to make the trees completly white.<br/>hope that was helpful</td>', 'Originally posted by ElGordo: Excellent work!  Your IR image really shows off the foliage well.  How did you manage to keep the sky such a beautiful blue?   i took many many shots with different aperture/exposure time.shot in raw, white balance in photoshop (incadescent), auto levels, and channel inversion. and hue /saturation to make the trees completly white.hope that was helpful', '2006-12-09 20:02:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3102948, 431533, 53278, '<td valign="top">Bob,<br/> <br/>i really like this shot a lot, but i think it could have been processed in another way. i think the real problem with it was it''s flat and a lot of edge sharpening. or maybe in this case texture effects created that.i am def. interested in seing the original!</td>', 'Bob, i really like this shot a lot, but i think it could have been processed in another way. i think the real problem with it was it''s flat and a lot of edge sharpening. or maybe in this case texture effects created that.i am def. interested in seing the original!', '2006-12-09 20:06:16.000000', NULL, 0),
