(3103537, 431973, 66840, '<td valign="top">I do agree that this picture deserved that 10.. i would have 10''d it also.. just the size is sooooooooo small... here''s an idea for you.. if you have windows xp  go to windows powertoys and find the image resizer.  it''s quick and you just download it, (it''s free) and right click on the image you want to resize and it will give you 4 options.  Small is the one I choose for this website cuz it''s 640x480 like what we should have.  And my pictures are sometimes smaller than others, but at least the right size.  It''s an awesome program to use and takes the confusion out of resizing (for me at least).  I hope I''ve given you some help on this.. I would LOVE to see the picture larger though.. it''s a GREAT SHOT!!!!</td>', 'I do agree that this picture deserved that 10.. i would have 10''d it also.. just the size is sooooooooo small... here''s an idea for you.. if you have windows xp  go to windows powertoys and find the image resizer.  it''s quick and you just download it, (it''s free) and right click on the image you want to resize and it will give you 4 options.  Small is the one I choose for this website cuz it''s 640x480 like what we should have.  And my pictures are sometimes smaller than others, but at least the right size.  It''s an awesome program to use and takes the confusion out of resizing (for me at least).  I hope I''ve given you some help on this.. I would LOVE to see the picture larger though.. it''s a GREAT SHOT!!!!', '2006-12-10 03:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3103606, 433516, 66398, '<td valign="top">I think if you look at the original of this photo (the thumb is now in the remarks section) you will see that I have grown quite a bit in the post processing area from my first photos entered. For the comments below on the haziness and color please take a look at the original. Yes it was a bit hazy (I can''t change the weather) and maybe there was more I could do on the coloring but, I think I improved quite a bit from the original.</td>', 'I think if you look at the original of this photo (the thumb is now in the remarks section) you will see that I have grown quite a bit in the post processing area from my first photos entered. For the comments below on the haziness and color please take a look at the original. Yes it was a bit hazy (I can''t change the weather) and maybe there was more I could do on the coloring but, I think I improved quite a bit from the original.', '2006-12-10 06:17:56.000000', NULL, 0),
